nly\nif the first nonzero <MATH_0010> is <MATH_0011>, or all <MATH_0012>.\nSo <MATH_0013>.\nThe subsets <MATH_0014> are prime ideals\nof <MATH_0015>, see Algebra, notation above\nLemma <REF_0003>. These together\nwith <MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> are the only prime ideals.\nHence <MATH_0018> is an example of a ring with the given structure of\nits spectrum, by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c6be3262c81ccf20847d119a613ed22dc4dcfca43d3e51387023d53db2af7429", "unit_id": "tag:01IY:statement"}
